### BLOCKERS — this attempt is REJECTED until every one is resolved
- [blocker] The onEntryChange callback hand-rolls ~40 lines of Contentstack query-building logic (ContentType().Entry().language().toJSON(), includeReference, only, except, fetch/findOne, jsonToHTML) that already exists in ContentstackFactory.createContentTypeEntryQuery / createContentTypeQuery and the exported getSingleEntry / getEntry / findSingletonEntry functions in src/services/contentstack.ts. The plan explicitly prescribes: 'The onEntryChange callback in _app.tsx should reuse the same getSingleEntry pattern (via ContentstackFactory.createContentTypeEntryQuery from src/services/contentstack.ts line 185) for client-side re-fetches.' The existing getSingleEntry function handles referenceFieldPath, only, except, jsonRtePath (with renderOption), and error logging — all duplicated here. The fix could be ~5 lines: set the preview hash on Stack.live_preview, then call getSingleEntry or findSingletonEntry. (src/pages/_app.tsx:75)
  - Suggested fix: Replace the hand-rolled query block with: `Stack.live_preview.live_preview = hash; const entry = entryUid ? await getSingleEntry({ contentTypeUid, entryUid, lang, ...contentstackConfig[contentTypeUid] }) : (await getEntry({ contentTypeUid, lang, ...contentstackConfig[contentTypeUid] }))[0];` Import getSingleEntry and getEntry from services/contentstack. This eliminates ~40 lines and fixes the jsonToHTML renderOption inconsistency.
### Advisory — apply where it makes the change smaller or clearer
- [major] The live_preview config uses `management_token` instead of the prescribed `preview_token`. The plan explicitly says: `live_preview: { enable: true, preview_token: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN || '' }`. The env var is named CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN (a preview token), but it is assigned to `management_token` (a different token type in the Contentstack SDK). If the SDK does not consume `management_token` in the live_preview config, live preview will silently not work at runtime. The test only verifies the mock was called with the object — it does not verify the SDK actually reads this key. (src/services/contentstack.ts:77)
  - Suggested fix: Use `preview_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN` as prescribed. If investigation shows the SDK requires `management_token`, document why with a comment and update the plan.
- [major] Hardcoded `host: 'api.contentstack.io'` in the live_preview config. Review criteria #6 requires all endpoint URLs to use named constants. The existing code already has `CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST` env var used with `Stack.setHost()`. The live_preview host should reuse the same constant or env var, not a string literal. (src/services/contentstack.ts:78)
  - Suggested fix: Use `host: CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST || 'api.contentstack.io'` or define a named constant in src/constants/contentstack.ts for the preview host.
- [major] ContentstackLivePreview.init() and onEntryChange() are called inside a useEffect with [locale] dependency. Every locale change re-initializes the live preview utility and registers a new onEntryChange callback without cleaning up the previous one. This can cause: (1) duplicate callbacks firing multiple fetches per entry change, (2) re-initialization side effects (DOM manipulation, internal state reset). The init() should run once on mount; the locale should be captured via a ref so the callback always reads the current value without re-registering. (src/pages/_app.tsx:48)
  - Suggested fix: Move ContentstackLivePreview.init() to a useEffect([]) (mount-only). Use a `const localeRef = useRef(locale); localeRef.current = locale;` pattern so the onEntryChange callback reads localeRef.current. Register onEntryChange once.
- [major] jsonToHTML is called without the renderOption parameter that src/services/contentstack.ts uses (line 152: `Utils.jsonToHTML({ entry: result, paths: jsonRtePath, renderOption })`). The renderOption defines span rendering behavior. Omitting it means JSON RTE fields in live preview will render differently from published content, causing visual inconsistency. This would be automatically fixed by reusing getSingleEntry/getEntry (see blocker). (src/pages/_app.tsx:113)
  - Suggested fix: Pass renderOption (export it from contentstack.ts) or reuse getSingleEntry/getEntry which already includes it.
- [minor] `livePreviewContent?: IContentstackContext | null` is a self-referential type — IContentstackContext contains a field of type IContentstackContext. This is confusing and semantically wrong: livePreviewContent holds partial entry data (e.g., `{ page: [entry] }`), not a full context. It should be `Partial<IContentstackContext>` or a dedicated type. (src/context/contentstackContext.tsx:21)
  - Suggested fix: Change to `livePreviewContent?: Partial<IContentstackContext> | null` or define a `LivePreviewData` type.
- [minor] `Stack.live_preview as unknown as Record<string, string> & { content_type_uid?: string; entry_uid?: string; }` uses a double cast (`as unknown as`) to bypass TypeScript. This is an untyped escape hatch. The Stack type from the contentstack SDK should be augmented or a proper interface declared for the live_preview shape. (src/pages/_app.tsx:62)
  - Suggested fix: Declare an interface for the live_preview internal shape and use a single cast, or augment the contentstack module's Stack type.
